VU1 FMAC kernels forced inline: normalizeLanes, classifyExact and arith in ps2_vu1_fmac.h are now __forceinline (always_inline elsewhere), and the dest lane reversal is a constexpr function (reverseLanes) as well as the table. A caller that passes a constant instruction word, as the compiled VU1 programs of a game port do, gets the register numbers and lane masks folded and the flag work it never reads dropped. Results are unchanged: the interpreter's FMAC fuzz check (200,000 instructions, specialized against general) and the replay of 105 recorded game runs stay exact.

